WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.300
Vision-language models can describe what happens in a video.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.250
But can they turn a stream of videos into reusable skills?

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.325
Meet Video2Skill.

00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:15.750
A model watches videos one after another, and keeps a persistent skill library.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:21.025
For every event, it must decide: reuse an existing skill, or create a new one.

00:00:21.325 --> 00:00:27.525
Our benchmark spans robot and human manipulation, with over twelve thousand verified skill calls.

00:00:27.825 --> 00:00:33.075
We tested 19 open-source VLMs. Many group events at near-chance level.

00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:39.150
Unified models merge distinct skills, while factorized models duplicate recurring ones.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:46.050
Fine-tuning, including our CLaRe method, improves grouping, but models still reuse far more than they create.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.525
Their libraries stall below half the reference size.

00:00:49.825 --> 00:00:54.175
The open challenge: recognizing when existing skills are not enough.

00:00:54.475 --> 00:00:57.700
Paper, code, and data are on our project page.
